# A ghost suggestion belongs to a typing mode. In vim's NORMAL mode a
# bare Tab is `buffer.next`, not "accept": the ghost is dropped and the
# buffer is untouched — the hunt once saw three list items land in a
# file nobody was typing in, with the `:` line open. In INSERT it lands.
write a.txt "banana\n"
open a.txt
command editor.use_vim
expect screen contains "NORMAL"
ghost "elderberry\nfig\ngrape"
key tab
expect screen lacks "elderberry"
expect dirty false
key :
ghost GHOSTED
key tab
expect dirty false
key esc
key i
expect screen contains "INSERT"
ghost "apple "
key tab
expect dirty true
command file.save
expect file a.txt contains "apple banana"
